 "notes": [
  "All six channel sets are statistically indistinguishable (subject-level Wilcoxon p >= 0.74 vs full); the motion subspace saturates: adding acc_ln/mag to acc+gyro changes per-window HR only in the 4th decimal (same comb peaks), so ch_full and ch_acc_gyro_mag MAEs coincide.",
  "LOSO channel law: best-single (acc wide in 7/8 folds, acc low-noise in 1/8) beats or ties full in 8/8 folds -> 'more channels is better' does NOT hold; a single accelerometer is sufficient and the sign is stable.",
  "Continuity prior HURTS on wrist motion segments (on-minus-off +4.91 bpm, p=0.64, n=8): direction consistent with activity-gated continuity; see BIDMC replication for the resting contrast.",
  "Original run_ablation.py design rows 'fs=32/16 Hz' had n=0 (kisr.stft crash when window < nperseg) and its rate labels were 2x off at 256 Hz; this run uses true 64/32/16 Hz with nperseg=fs."
 ],
